diff --git a/tools/patches/history/0012-exclude-offpump-presents.patch b/tools/patches/history/0012-exclude-offpump-presents.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3aa2833
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/patches/history/0012-exclude-offpump-presents.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,224 @@
+From b765a1f8d76619da8583f7ac512621fbfb55dfa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: luoye-cpu <3412829159@qq.com>
+Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:16:26 +0800
+Subject: [PATCH] fix(render): exclude the last two off-pump Presents so the
+ pump is the only presenter
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+docs/39 §3.3 listed two remaining exceptions to "only one thread in the process
+is inside IDXGISwapChain::Present": ClearSurface()'s Present(0, 0) on the caller
+thread and PresentTimedText()'s 2 s handoff-timeout fallback. The single-pump
+change took the 4-route crash rate from 8/8 to 0/8, but a re-run with the
+observability counters in place produced 1 crash in 8 — and the counters point
+at exactly these two: ClearSurface fired 4 times per 8 smoke runs (all four
+routes clustered within ~1 ms in app-2026-09-20.log), the handoff timeout never
+fired.
+
+ClearSurface (option B, skip): ResetMedia() and Close() both call
+StopPresentationPumpMembership() before taking deviceMutex_, so this renderer is
+already out of the pump when the clear runs and no later pump round will compose
+for it — a "present it next round" hand-off is not available without
+re-registering a renderer that is being torn down. What matters is that another
+route's pump round is inside Present at that moment. Gating on "is the pump
+idle?" would not close it either (several closers can all observe members_ ==
+empty and then Present concurrently), so the Present is skipped unconditionally:
+the clear, the resource release and the lock order are untouched, only the
+Present is removed. Nothing stale can leak into a later frame — every compose
+path fully repaints the back buffer first (DrawCachedVideo clears the target).
+
+Handoff timeout: the wait stays bounded at 2 s (the caller is never stalled for
+good) but no longer falls back to Presenting from the caller thread. Reaching it
+means the pump has not finished a round in five times the worst round measured
+(372.9 ms), i.e. the device is in trouble; a second presenter pipeline on a
+device in that state is the most dangerous and least useful thing to do. The
+pending flag stays set, so the pump still presents the frame when it unwedges,
+and the caller returns DeviceFailure — which both call sites already handle by
+requesting device recovery (PlayerSession.cpp:672 / :2900).
+
+Counters kept for verification: offPumpClearSurfacePresents_ and
+handoffTimeoutFallbacks_ now count excluded Present requests instead of off-pump
+Presents, and the log line is "pump-owned Present excluded ..." — the former
+"off-pump Present ..." line no longer exists in the binary.
+
+Files: FFF.Native/3FP/Render/VideoRenderer.cpp, VideoRenderer.h
+---
+ FFF.Native/3FP/Render/VideoRenderer.cpp | 94 ++++++++++++++++++-------
+ FFF.Native/3FP/Render/VideoRenderer.h   | 13 ++--
+ 2 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)
